/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  unsteady05_tank_valve_drain -- a SELF-REGULATING level.

  A water tank drained through a valve, with NO controller.  The inflow steps
  from 0.20 to 0.30 kmol/s (a 50 % step, applied at t = 0 by starting the
  tank at the steady level of the OLD inflow and feeding the NEW one -- the
  initial-condition step of unsteady02), and the level climbs to a new
  steady level by itself, because the outflow grows with the level:

      Q = Cv x opening x sqrt(dP / rho)            [m3/s]
      dP = P + rho g h - P_downstream              (static head + vessel
                                                    pressure - downstream)
      F_out = Q rho / MW                           [kmol/s]
      A rho/MW dh/dt = F_in - F_out                (mass balance, the level
                                                    is volume / area)

  Here the vessel is open to the same pressure the valve discharges to
  (P = P_downstream = 1 atm), so the head alone drives the flow and the
  steady state F_out = F_in has a closed form:

      h* = (Q / (Cv x))^2 / g          with Q = F_in MW / rho

  Cv is the valve's effective flow AREA in m2 (the orifice equation's Cd A),
  `opening` the fraction of the stroke (linear), the outlet is at the bottom.
  Because Q ~ sqrt(h), h* grows with the SQUARE of the inflow: a 1.5-fold
  step in the inflow gives a 2.25-fold step in the level (0.998 m -> 2.245 m
  at rho = 1001.55 kg/m3, the package's own density at 293.15 K: the water
  record's Vliq at 25 C with Rackett supplying the temperature shape).  The engine
  prints this closed form at start-up; the run's own final level, read from
  trajectory.csv (column `level`), agrees with it to < 1e-3.

  WHAT TO SEE.  A first-order-like response with tau ~ 2600 s at the new
  level (linearising Q about h*: tau = A / (dQ/dh) = 2 A h* / Q).  Compare
  with ctrl21: with a manipulated OUTFLOW instead of a valve the same tank
  has NO such tendency -- it integrates the difference of the flows without
  bound, and only a level controller closes the loop.

  ENERGY.  The tank stores H on the elements datum (the package's mixture
  liquid surface) and T is a readout; the feed arrives at the tank's own
  temperature, so T stays at 293.15 K and the first-law ledger closes (see
  the `[balance]` lines and check_dynamic_tank).
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

units
(
    {
        name        tank;
        type        dynamicTank;
        in          feed;
        outputs     ( drain );

        operation
        {
            geometry
            {
                shape       verticalCylinder;
                diameter    2.0 m;              // area 3.1416 m2
                height      4.0 m;              // the overflow level
            }

            outflow
            {
                mode        valve;
                opening     0.5;
                valve
                {
                    Cv                  2.3e-3 m2;      // effective flow area (Cd A)
                    downstreamPressure  101325.0 Pa;
                }
            }
        }
    }
);
